id: 24
hanzi: 好客
pinyin: hào kè
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Adjective

meanings_summary:
  en: hospitable; friendly to visitors; fond of entertaining guests
  es: hospitalario; acogedor; generoso con las visitas; amante de agasajar

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Adjective | Standard | enthusiastic, warm, and generous in receiving, entertaining, and lodging guests | cálido, entusiasta y desprendido al recibir, atender y alojar a los visitantes | 热情好客的主人 (warm and hospitable host)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 草原上的牧民纯朴好客，每当有远方的客人骑马到来，总会端出喷香的奶茶和手把肉热情款待。 | Cǎoyuán shàng de mùmín chūnpǔ hàokè, měidāng yǒu yuǎnfāng de kèrén qǐmǎ dàolái, zǒng huì duānchū pēnxiāng de nǎichá hé shǒubàròu rèqíng kuǎndài. | Herdsmen on the grassland are simple and hospitable; whenever travelers arrive on horseback, they serve fragrant milk tea and mutton cordially. | Los pastores de la estepa son hospitalarios y llanos; al llegar viajeros a caballo, siempre sirven té con leche aromático y carnes asadas.
  #2 | 鲁迅在北京与上海居住期间极度好客，家中常常高朋满座，同乡挚友与求教青年络绎不绝。 | Lǔ Xùn zài Běijīng yǔ Shànghǎi jūzhù qījiān jídù hàokè, jiā zhōng chángcháng gāopéng-mǎnzuò, tóngxiāng zhìyǒu yǔ qiújiào qīngnián luòyì-bùjué. | Lu Xun was exceptionally hospitable in Beijing and Shanghai; his home was constantly filled with distinguished friends and visiting youths. | Lu Xun fue un anfitrión entrañable en Pekín y Shanghái; su morada paraba colmada de paisanos, amigos dilectos y jóvenes aprendices.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  热情好客 | warm and hospitable
  生性好客 | naturally hospitable by disposition
  好客之邦 | a nation known for hospitality
  好客的民风 | hospitable folk customs
  淳朴好客 | honest, simple, and hospitable
  好客的主人家 | hospitable host family

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  倾囊相助 | qīng náng xiāng zhù | empty one's purse to assist a friend in need
  高朋满座 | gāo péng mǎn zuò | a hall full of distinguished and noble guests
  投桃报李 | tóu táo bào lǐ | return a plum when given a peach; reciprocate mutual goodwill
  倒屣相迎 | dào xǐ xiāng yíng | rush out with shoes on backwards in eager welcome

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  好 | hào | be fond of; love; like (4th tone) | amar; gustar; ser aficionado a (4to tono) | 女 | woman | 女 (woman/mother) | 子 (child) | 6 | 左右结构 | Ancient oracle bone pictogram showing a loving mother 女 embracing her newborn child 子; pronounced hào when expressing fondness. | A fond mother (女) lovingly cradles her sweet child (子), showing deep affection and love (好). | Una madre abnegada (女) abraza a su pequeño (子), reflejando entrañable apego y gusto (好). | 51 | VND | ""
  客 | kè | guest; visitor; traveler; customer | huésped; invitado; forastero; cliente | 宀 | roof | 宀 (sheltering roof) | 各 (gè, arrival of person from another place) | 9 | 上下结构 | Ideogram showing an individual 各 from another location arriving under the household roof 宀 as a respected guest. | Under the warm roof (宀), travelers from various regions (各) are welcomed as honored guests (客). | Bajo el alero hospitalario (宀), visitantes de diversos confines (各) son acogidos como huéspedes (客). | 51 | JHER | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A generous heart that loves (好, hào) to welcome travelers under the roof as guests (客) is truly hospitable (好客).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Quien ama de corazón (好, hào) recibir a viajeros bajo su techo como huéspedes (客) es hospitalario (好客).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Derived from classical Chinese virtue ethics; in ancient China, hosting traveling scholars and wanderers (养客) was considered the supreme badge of chivalric honor and generosity.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Two falling tones: 'hào kè' (51-51). Note the crucial 4th tone on 'hào' (meaning 'to be fond of'); do not pronounce as 3rd tone hǎo.

