    宾 | bīn | esteemed guest; visitor at court
    朋 | péng | friend; companion; two strings of cowries
    友 | yǒu | friend; two clasped hands

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 好客 specifically characterizes an enthusiastic, warm disposition toward entertaining visitors and treating guests well.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 好客 vs. 热情 | rèqíng | 热情 is a broad personality trait describing general warmth, zeal, or energy in any situation, while 好客 is restricted to receiving guests and travelers.
    2 | 好客 vs. 友善 | yǒushàn | 友善 means amicable and kind to others, whereas 好客 specifically implies opening one's home and table to visitors.
    3 | 好客 vs. 周到 | zhōudào | 周到 emphasizes thorough, flawless attentiveness in service or protocol, while 好客 emphasizes genuine emotional enthusiasm for guests.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 山里人天性纯朴好客，哪怕家境并不宽裕，逢有陌生旅人借宿，也总会杀鸡宰鸭拿出最好的存粮款待。围坐在暖融融的柴火堆旁，听着老人讲述山间古老的传说，那种毫无防备的赤诚与善意，足以驱散长途跋涉的所有严寒。 | Shānlǐ rén tiānxìng chūnpǔ hàokè, nǎpà jiājìng bìng bù kuānyù, féng yǒu mòshēng lǚrén jièsù, yě zǒng huì shājī-zǎiyā ná chū zuì hǎo de cúnliáng kuǎndài. Wéizuò zài nuǎnróngróng de cháihuǒduī páng, tīng zhe lǎorén jiǎngshù shānjiān gǔlǎo de chuánshuō, nà zhǒng háowú-fángbèi de chìchéng yǔ shànyì, zúyǐ qūsàn chángtú bǎshè de suǒyǒu yánhán. | Mountain folk are naturally hospitable; even with modest means, when strangers seek shelter they prepare their best provisions. Sitting by the crackling woodfire listening to mountain legends, their warmth dispels all chills of the journey. | Los montañeses son hospitalarios por naturaleza; aun con pocos recursos, ante un viajero perdido preparan sus mejores viandas. Al calor del fuego de leña, escuchando viejas leyendas, su generosa calidez disipa el frío del camino.
  #2 | “好客中国”不仅是享誉世界的国家旅游名片，更是中华优秀传统文化中“有朋自远方来，不亦乐乎”的当代传承。在各大国际经贸展会与体育盛事中，志愿者们以真诚热忱的好客之礼迎接四海宾朋，向世界生动展现了礼仪之邦的大国风范。 | 'Hàokè Zhōngguó' bùjǐn shì xiǎngyù shìjiè de guójiā lǚyóu míngpiàn, gèng shì Zhōnghuá yōuxiù chuántǒng wénhuà zhōng 'yǒu péng zì yuǎnfāng lái, bú yì lè hū' de dāngdài chuánchéng. Zài gèdà guójì jīngmào zhǎnhuì yǔ tǐyù shèngshì zhōng, zhìyuànzhěmen yǐ zhēnchéng rèchén de hàokè zhī lǐ yíngjiē sìhǎi bīnpéng, xiàng shìjiè shēngdòng zhǎnxiàn le lǐyí-zhī-bāng de dàguó fēngfàn. | 'Hospitable China' reflects the ancient teaching: 'To have friends come from afar, is this not delightful?' In international expos and tournaments, volunteers greet global guests with sincere hospitality, displaying civilizational elegance. | 'China hospitalaria' evoca el milenario lema de Confucio: '¿No es un gozo recibir amigos de tierras lejanas?'. En cumbres y torneos internacionales, los voluntarios acogen al forastero con afabilidad, mostrando la hidalguía de una nación de protocolo.
